 "brief": "A writer and political analyst told Shehab Wire that the killing of Colonel Jamal Abu Kamil, director of the Gaza police force, represents part of a broader scheme aimed at undermining civilian stability and fracturing social cohesion in the territory. The analyst characterized the assassination as a crime committed by the occupation intended to justify further violations and break down institutional trust.\n\nThe targeted killing of police leadership follows a pattern designed to weaken internal unity across Gaza's civilian institutions, the analyst said. Such operations serve to destabilize the security sector and dismantle the institutional frameworks that sustain public order within the territory, he added.",
